## In vivo experiments
Animals. Female Kunming mice (8 weeks old, $29.8\ \pm\ 1.5\ \mathrm{g})$ were used for uranium decorporation studies. All animal assays were approved by the Animal Care and Use Committee of Soochow University.
In vivo uranium decorporation assays. U(VI) solution in standard injectable dosage $({\dot{0}}.5~{\mathrm{mg}}^{~238}{\mathsf{U}}({\mathsf{V}}{\mathsf{I}}){\mathsf{/k g}})$ was prepared by dissolving $^{2\bar{3}8}\mathsf{U O}_{2}(\mathsf{N O}_{3})_{2}{\cdot}6\mathsf{\bar{H}}_{2}\bar{0}$ $(3.2~\mathsf{m g})$ in $20.0~\mathrm{mL}$ of physiological saline $[0.14\ \mathrm{mol/L}\ \mathsf{N a C l})$ . The ligand solutions were prepared by dispersing and sonicating $Z n N a_{3}$ -DTPA $(21.0\ \mathsf{m g})$ , 3,2-HOPO-COOH $(4.3~\mathsf{m g})$ , $M\mathsf{I L}\mathsf{-}\mathsf{101-N H}_{2}$ $(16.2~\mathsf{m g})$ , or MIL-101-HOPO $\left(21.0~\mathsf{m g}\right)$ each in $1.4~\mathsf{m L}$ of physiological saline. All solutions were adjusted to $\mathsf{p H}7-8$ with $0.1\mathsf{m o l/L N a O H}$ .
First, 25 mice were randomly divided into five groups, and then, $0.2~\mathsf{m L}$ of decorporation agent or physiological saline was administered intravenously to each mouse $\boldsymbol{[Z\mathsf{n N a}_{3}}$ -DTPA 100.0 mg/kg; 3,2-HOPO-COOH, $20.5{\mathrm{~mg/kg}};$ MIL-101- ${\mathsf{N H}}_{2}$ , $77.3~\mathsf{m g}/\mathsf{k g};$ MIL-101-HOPO, $100.0\ \mathrm{mg/kg)}$ , and $0.2~\mathsf{m L}$ of U(VI) solution was given to each mouse $(0.5~\mathrm{mg/kg)}$ in the same manner $1\mathfrak{h}$ later. All mice were given water and food $4h$ later and sacrificed $24\ h$ after the U(VI) injection. The kidneys and femurs were obtained, weighed and digested by a microwave digestion apparatus (MASTER-40, Sineo Microwave Chemistry Technology), and the U(VI) concentration of tissue samples was measured by ICP-MS.
