## Cell experiments
Cell line and culture. NRK-52E (obtained from the Chinese Academy of Sciences) was cultured in the DMEM/F-12 (Gibco, Thermo Scientific), which is a culture medium supplemented with $10\%$ (V/V) fetal bovine serum (FBS) (Gibco, Thermo Scientific) and $1\%$ penicillin–streptomycin, and grown in a humid atmosphere containing $5\%$ ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ at $37^{\circ}\mathsf C$ . The cells were propagated every two days.
Cell cytotoxicity assays. NRK-52E cells in log phase were cultured in 96-well plates with 4000 cells per well and incubated for $24\ h$ . The cells were then exposed to various concentrations (3.125, 6.25, 12.5, 25, 50, and $100~\mathrm{\upmug/mL})$ of $Z n N a_{3}$ -DTPA, 3,2-HOPO-COOH, $M\mathsf{l}\mathsf{L}\mathsf{-}\mathsf{1}0\mathsf{1}\mathsf{-}\mathsf{N}\mathsf{H}_{2},$ or MIL-101-HOPO, with 12.4 μmol/L of uranyl nitrate, respectively, while the control group was only treated with culture medium. After continuous incubation for $48\ h$ , $10~\upmu\upiota$ CCK-8 reagent was added per well and the cells were cultured for another $2h$ . The optical density (OD) of every well was obtained at $450\ \mathsf{n m}$ by ELISA (FilterMax F5). The survival rate was calculated using the formula: [ODexperimental– $-0\mathsf{D}_{\mathsf{b l a n k}}]/[0\mathsf{D}_{\mathsf{c o n t r o l}}-$ $\mathsf{O D}_{\mathsf{b l a n k}}]\times100\%$ . All the independent experiments were statistically tested with SPSS.
